No nonnull, dereferenceable or align on `this` for Apple platforms, as Xcode 27.0's clang compiles them with
-clang-vendor-feature=+thisNoNullAttr and +thisNoAlignAttr, which its driver passes for Apple targets only (B-170,
docs/formats/build.md "Objective-C literals, runtime entrypoints and `this`"). Written from Xcode's observed output (.github/scripts/clang_objc_experiments.py).

diff --git a/clang/lib/CodeGen/CGCall.cpp b/clang/lib/CodeGen/CGCall.cpp
index 942e9d79..d188cd32 100644
--- a/clang/lib/CodeGen/CGCall.cpp
+++ b/clang/lib/CodeGen/CGCall.cpp
@@ -2775,10 +2775,12 @@ void CodeGenModule::ConstructAttributeList(StringRef Name,
   }
 
   // Apply `nonnull`, `dereferenceable(N)` and `align N` to the `this` argument,
-  // unless this is a thunk function.
+  // unless this is a thunk function. Xcode 27.0's clang gives `this` none of
+  // them for Apple platforms (its thisNoNullAttr and thisNoAlignAttr).
   // FIXME: fix this properly, https://reviews.llvm.org/D100388
   if (FI.isInstanceMethod() && !IRFunctionArgs.hasInallocaArg() &&
-      !FI.arg_begin()->type->isVoidPointerType() && !IsThunk) {
